New defect (blocker F1r2, committed as the failing guard adv 9,
scripts/__tests__/oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts:1621):
- oxlint honors two directive forms that the pin and the sweep do not see:
  a mid-line block disable (code before the comment on the same line, for
  example "const keep = 1; /* eslint-disable */") and a block disable that
  spans lines ("/* eslint-disable\n */"). Live proof under
  apps/integrated-math-3: each seeded form exits 0 under the root config
  while the paired bare control exits 1 with eslint(no-unused-vars).
- Why the guard misses them: WHOLE_LINE_DISABLE_RE
  (scripts/__tests__/oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts:901) requires the comment
  to close its own line, and the trailing branch of directiveKindsOfFile
  (:996) matches only // forms, so directiveKindsOfFile (:981) counts
  neither form. stripDisableComments (:907) strips neither form, so the
  sweep lints the copy with the comment still in place and never surfaces
  the hidden rule. The kinds, count, and blanket-block pins stay
  unchanged. A listed carrier file can therefore hide a new live finding
  without failing adv 7. The guard comment "a new blanket block ... fail
  adv 7" (:958) is false for these two blanket forms.
- The real tree holds neither form today: rg over the source files of
  apps/ and packages/ finds exactly one non-whole-line directive, the
  trailing // eslint-disable-line at
  apps/bus-math-v2/hooks/usePhaseCompletion.ts:148. The hole is latent,
  not live.
- Green must extend the directive counting and the strip to mid-line and
  multi-line block comments in both spellings, so adv 9 passes.

